      "side": 1,
      "message": "The extra level of nesting to assign `None` to `None` (if `self.prop.is_none()`) is confusing; why not simply:\n```suggestion\n        let res \u003d self.prop?;\n\n        self.prop \u003d res.next().ok()?;\n```\n\n\nAlso, note that, if `next().is_err()`, we don\u0027t update `self.prop` so that this `Iterator` will retry the call on the following `next`, which might not fail anymore, violating the expected Rust `Iterator` behavior. This is why I was using `.ok().flatten()` instead of `.ok()?` in a similar comment some time ago: if we get `Err()` once, we return `None` forever after.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 344,
        "startChar": 0,
